      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Considering your PNW soil pH and compost addition, I'd recommend using bone meal over blood meal. Bone meal tends to have a more gradual release of nitrogen and is less likely to cause pH spikes, making it a better option for your soil. Blood meal, on the other hand, can be more acidic and may further lower your pH, exacerbating the existing issue.",
