      "content": "While chemical and microbiological factors are crucial, there are indeed other aspects of soil health that reside beneath the surface of what we can measure. Soils have been described as \"ecosystems on earth\" and exhibit complex patterns of activity that defy direct observation, such as soil maceration, topotactic remolding, and solutions-based transport of soil nutrients. These processes involve dynamic interactions between soil particles, water, air, and living organisms that shape the structure and chemistry of the soil, influencing plant growth and soil sustainability.",
